{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-job-037",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 37,
  "title": "Job 37",
  "display_title": "Job 37",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "job",
  "book": "Job",
  "bookName": "Job",
  "bookOrder": 18,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 37,
  "sortOrder": 18037,
  "verseCount": 24,
  "aliases": [
    "Job"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "At this also my heart trembleth, and is moved out of his place.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Hear attentively the noise of his voice, and the sound that goeth out of his mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "He directeth it under the whole heaven, and his lightning unto the ends of the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "After it a voice roareth: he thundereth with the voice of his excellency; and he will not stay them when his voice is heard.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "God thundereth marvellously with his voice; great things doeth he, which we cannot comprehend.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "For he saith to the snow, Be thou on the earth; likewise to the small rain, and to the great rain of his strength.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "He sealeth up the hand of every man; that all men may know his work.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Then the beasts go into dens, and remain in their places.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Out of the south cometh the whirlwind: and cold out of the north.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "By the breath of God frost is given: and the breadth of the waters is straitened.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "Also by watering he wearieth the thick cloud: he scattereth his bright cloud:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "And it is turned round about by his counsels: that they may do whatsoever he commandeth them upon the face of the world in the earth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "He causeth it to come, whether for correction, or for his land, or for mercy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "Hearken unto this, O Job: stand still, and consider the wondrous works of God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "Dost thou know when God disposed them, and caused the light of his cloud to shine?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "Dost thou know the balancings of the clouds, the wondrous works of him which is perfect in knowledge?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "How thy garments are warm, when he quieteth the earth by the south wind?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "Hast thou with him spread out the sky, which is strong, and as a molten looking glass?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "Teach us what we shall say unto him; for we cannot order our speech by reason of darkness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Shall it be told him that I speak? if a man speak, surely he shall be swallowed up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "And now men see not the bright light which is in the clouds: but the wind passeth, and cleanseth them.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "Fair weather cometh out of the north: with God is terrible majesty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "Touching the Almighty, we cannot find him out: he is excellent in power, and in judgment, and in plenty of justice: he will not afflict.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:job:37:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "Men do therefore fear him: he respecteth not any that are wise of heart.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Job 37:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:job:37:24"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
